    "answer": "The Clean Supplier Report indicates that the normal security posture of a supplier includes using basic authentication methods to secure systems or applications. The report also notes that this particular supplier maintains audit logs with an active retention period of thirty days, which is essential for monitoring and investigating any potential incidents related to access control failures within their environment. Furthermore, it suggests enhancing file access controls by implementing additional measures such as file integrity checks (e.g., using tools like Tripwire) or employing a Data Loss Prevention solution that can help detect unauthorized data transfers both inside the network perimeter and externally.\n\nHowever, it's important for organizations to note that this report is part of an internal demo exercise. It does not contain any operational instructions aimed at improving security measures within their own systems but rather serves as educational content on best practices in supplier management."
